<div id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and fixed <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, set</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\gamma}(s):=P_{t-s}\mathrm{e}^{\gamma u_{s}},\qquad 0\leq s\leq t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\gamma}(s):=P_{t-s}\mathrm{e}^{\gamma u_{s}},\qquad 0\leq s\leq t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">The Nemytskii map <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\mapsto\mathrm{e}^{\gamma v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\mapsto\mathrm{e}^{\gamma v}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously Fréchet differentiable on
<math id="S4.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}(V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}(V)</annotation></semantics></math>, with derivative <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\mapsto\gamma\mathrm{e}^{\gamma v}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\mapsto\gamma\mathrm{e}^{\gamma v}h</annotation></semantics></math>; on bounded subsets its
derivative is bounded and locally Lipschitz. Since <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C^{1}([0,\infty),\ell^{\infty})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C^{1}([0,\infty),\ell^{\infty})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable in operator norm, <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as an
