ion encoding="application/x-tex">s=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=t</annotation></semantics></math> gives (<a href="#S4.E41" title="In Proposition 4.3 (Semigroup comparisons). ‣ 4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E42" title="In Proposition 4.3 (Semigroup comparisons). ‣ 4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>).
