<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Li–Yau and Harnack estimates</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Münch’s finite-graph maximum-principle calculation gives the modified Li–Yau estimate
under <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CD}(0,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CD</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CD}(0,n)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, Theorem 3.1]</cite>; Pajot and Russ adapted that argument
to infinite bounded-geometry graphs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, Section 7.1]</cite>. The proof below follows this
scheme, with the global finite-dimensional curvature term replaced by the extremal point-mass
estimate from Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Extremal curvature–dimension inequality). ‣ 3.1. Point-mass estimates ‣ 3. Point-mass estimates and resolvent smoothing ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and with a distance penalisation that makes
the <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> argument valid without a volume-growth assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The extremal estimate in Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Extremal curvature–dimension inequality). ‣ 3.1. Point-mass estimates ‣ 3. Point-mass estimates and resolvent smoothing ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, rather than a global finite-dimensional condition, is enough to prove the modified Li–Yau inequality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Modified Li–Yau inequality)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution in Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Global nonlinear flow and gradient bound). ‣ 4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(45)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\Delta u_{t}(x)\leq\frac{N}{2t}\qquad(x\in V,\ t&gt;0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\Delta u_{t}(x)\leq\frac{N}{2t}\qquad(x\in V,\ t&gt;0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We give a proof that covers infinite graphs without any a priori growth assumption. Fix a root <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, put</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(x):=\operatorname{dist}(o,x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(x):=\operatorname{dist}(o,x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">and fix <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The boundedness of <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>, together with boundedness of <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> on
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}(V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}(V)</annotation></semantics></math>, implies that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(t,x):=t\Delta u_{t}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(t,x):=t\Delta u_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">is bounded on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]\times V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]\times V</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}u=\Delta u+\Gamma(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}u=\Delta u+\Gamma(u)</annotation></semantics></math>; the boundedness and bilinearity recorded above imply that
the vector field <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in the
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm. Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto t\Delta u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto t\Delta u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously differentiable in
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}(V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}(V)</annotation></semantics></math>, which justifies the time derivative used at the penalised minimum. For <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, consider</span></p>
<table id="S4.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(46)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t,x):=\Psi(t,x)+\varepsilon\rho(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t,x):=\Psi(t,x)+\varepsilon\rho(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">This function attains a global minimum on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]\times V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]\times V</annotation></semantics></math>. The assertion is immediate when <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is finite. When <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite, put</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{T}:=\sup_{[0,T]\times V}\left\lvert\Psi\right\rvert&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{T}:=\sup_{[0,T]\times V}\left\lvert\Psi\right\rvert&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\varepsilon}(0,o)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\varepsilon}(0,o)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t,x)\geq-M_{T}+\varepsilon\rho(x)&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t,x)\geq-M_{T}+\varepsilon\rho(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">if <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(x)&gt;M_{T}/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(x)&gt;M_{T}/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the infimum over <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]\times V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]\times V</annotation></semantics></math> equals the minimum over <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math> times a finite ball and is therefore attained.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose first that the minimum is negative, and let <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{\varepsilon},x_{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{\varepsilon},x_{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> be a minimiser. Then <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\varepsilon}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\varepsilon}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S4.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(47)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\Delta u_{t_{\varepsilon}}(x_{\varepsilon})&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\Delta u_{t_{\varepsilon}}(x_{\varepsilon})&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\varepsilon}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\varepsilon}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>, the time derivative of <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\Delta u_{t}(x_{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\Delta u_{t}(x_{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes. If <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\varepsilon}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\varepsilon}=T</annotation></semantics></math>, its left derivative is nonpositive; because the solution is <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> beyond <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, this left derivative equals the ordinary derivative at <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus in either case</span></p>
<table id="S4.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(48)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left.\partial_{t}^{-}\bigl(t\Delta u_{t}(x_{\varepsilon})\bigr)\right|_{t=t_{\varepsilon}}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><msub><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.\partial_{t}^{-}\bigl(t\Delta u_{t}(x_{\varepsilon})\bigr)\right|_{t=t_{\varepsilon}}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Spatial minimality and the fact that <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz give, for every <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\sim x_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\sim x_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(49)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta u_{t_{\varepsilon}}(y)-m\geq-\frac{\varepsilon}{t_{\varepsilon}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta u_{t_{\varepsilon}}(y)-m\geq-\frac{\varepsilon}{t_{\varepsilon}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Applying (<a href="#S3.E19" title="In Proposition 3.3 (Extremal curvature–dimension inequality). ‣ 3.1. Point-mass estimates ‣ 3. Point-mass estimates and resolvent smoothing ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) with <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\varepsilon/t_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\varepsilon/t_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then using <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x_{\varepsilon}}\leq d_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x_{\varepsilon}}\leq d_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x_{\varepsilon}}(d_{x_{\varepsilon}}+3)\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x_{\varepsilon}}(d_{x_{\varepsilon}}+3)\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(50)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{2}(u_{t_{\varepsilon}})(x_{\varepsilon})\geq\frac{1}{N}\left(-m-\frac{d_{*}\varepsilon}{2t_{\varepsilon}}\right)_{+}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{2}(u_{t_{\varepsilon}})(x_{\varepsilon})\geq\frac{1}{N}\left(-m-\frac{d_{*}\varepsilon}{2t_{\varepsilon}}\right)_{+}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In 2. Preliminary ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{t}(t\Delta u_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{t}(t\Delta u_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta u_{t}+t\bigl(\Delta^{2}u_{t}+\Delta\Gamma(u_{t})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta u_{t}+t\bigl(\Delta^{2}u_{t}+\Delta\Gamma(u_{t})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(51)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta u_{t}+t\bigl(\Delta^{2}u_{t}+2\Gamma(u_{t},\Delta u_{t})+2\Gamma_{2}(u_{t})\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta u_{t}+t\bigl(\Delta^{2}u_{t}+2\Gamma(u_{t},\Delta u_{t})+2\Gamma_{2}(u_{t})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">In the next two displays, all functions are evaluated at time <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. At <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> the transport part is</span></p>
<table id="S4.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(52)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}u+2\Gamma(u,\Delta u)=\sum_{y\sim x_{\varepsilon}}\bigl(\Delta u(y)-m\bigr)\bigl(1+u(y)-u(x_{\varepsilon})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}u+2\Gamma(u,\Delta u)=\sum_{y\sim x_{\varepsilon}}\bigl(\Delta u(y)-m\bigr)\bigl(1+u(y)-u(x_{\varepsilon})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Every second factor belongs to <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,2]</annotation></semantics></math> by (<a href="#S4.E33" title="In Proposition 4.1 (Global nonlinear flow and gradient bound). ‣ 4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>). Hence (<a href="#S4.E49" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) implies</span></p>
<table id="S4.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(53)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}u+2\Gamma(u,\Delta u)\geq-\frac{2d_{*}\varepsilon}{t_{\varepsilon}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}u+2\Gamma(u,\Delta u)\geq-\frac{2d_{*}\varepsilon}{t_{\varepsilon}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#S4.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>), (<a href="#S4.E50" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>), (<a href="#S4.E51" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>), and (<a href="#S4.E53" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>), and setting</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z:=-t_{\varepsilon}m&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z:=-t_{\varepsilon}m&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S4.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(54)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\geq-z-2d_{*}\varepsilon t_{\varepsilon}+\frac{2}{N}\left(z-\frac{d_{*}\varepsilon}{2}\right)_{+}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\geq-z-2d_{*}\varepsilon t_{\varepsilon}+\frac{2}{N}\left(z-\frac{d_{*}\varepsilon}{2}\right)_{+}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\varepsilon}:=\frac{d_{*}\varepsilon}{2},\qquad b_{\varepsilon}:=2d_{*}\varepsilon T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\varepsilon}:=\frac{d_{*}\varepsilon}{2},\qquad b_{\varepsilon}:=2d_{*}\varepsilon T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leq a_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leq a_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bound below is automatic. Otherwise <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w:=z-a_{\varepsilon}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w:=z-a_{\varepsilon}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2w^{2}}{N}\leq w+a_{\varepsilon}+b_{\varepsilon}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2w^{2}}{N}\leq w+a_{\varepsilon}+b_{\varepsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="S4.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(55)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leq a_{\varepsilon}+\frac{N}{4}\left(1+\sqrt{1+\frac{8(a_{\varepsilon}+b_{\varepsilon})}{N}}\right)=\frac{N}{2}+o_{\varepsilon\downarrow 0}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leq a_{\varepsilon}+\frac{N}{4}\left(1+\sqrt{1+\frac{8(a_{\varepsilon}+b_{\varepsilon})}{N}}\right)=\frac{N}{2}+o_{\varepsilon\downarrow 0}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text">At the minimiser,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t_{\varepsilon},x_{\varepsilon})=-z+\varepsilon\rho(x_{\varepsilon})\geq-z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t_{\varepsilon},x_{\varepsilon})=-z+\varepsilon\rho(x_{\varepsilon})\geq-z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.10.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, for every fixed <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,x)\in[0,T]\times V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,x)\in[0,T]\times V</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(56)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t\Delta u_{t}(x)\geq{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t\Delta u_{t}(x)\geq{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-a_{\varepsilon}-\frac{N}{4}\left(1+\sqrt{1+\frac{8(a_{\varepsilon}+b_{\varepsilon})}{N}}\right)-\varepsilon\rho(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-a_{\varepsilon}-\frac{N}{4}\left(1+\sqrt{1+\frac{8(a_{\varepsilon}+b_{\varepsilon})}{N}}\right)-\varepsilon\rho(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.11.1" class="ltx_text">If the minimum of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonnegative instead, then <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t,x)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\varepsilon}(t,x)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,x)</annotation></semantics></math>, so (<a href="#S4.E56" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) is immediate. Thus (<a href="#S4.E56" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) holds for every <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, regardless of the sign of the penalised minimum. Letting <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\Delta u_{t}(x)\geq-\frac{N}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\Delta u_{t}(x)\geq-\frac{N}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.12.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> was arbitrary, (<a href="#S4.E45" title="In Theorem 4.4 (Modified Li–Yau inequality). ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The passage from the differential estimate to Harnack control uses the graph path-and-time
splitting argument of Bauer et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Section 5]</cite> and, in the modified-flow setting,
the implementations of Münch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, Theorem 3.2]</cite> and Pajot and Russ
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, Section 7.2]</cite>. The one-dimensional estimate below is the minimal-integral
estimate of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Lemma 5.3]</cite>, in the form recorded in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, Lemma 5.3]</cite>. We include a direct proof to fix the constants and to make
explicit that only continuity of the scalar function is required.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-dimensional optimisation)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:[s_{1},s_{2}]\to[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:[s_{1},s_{2}]\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> be continuous. Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(57)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{s\in[s_{1},s_{2}]}\left\{\sqrt{2a(s)}-\int_{s}^{s_{2}}a(t)\,\,\mathrm{d}t\right\}\leq\frac{2}{s_{2}-s_{1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{s\in[s_{1},s_{2}]}\left\{\sqrt{2a(s)}-\int_{s}^{s_{2}}a(t)\,\,\mathrm{d}t\right\}\leq\frac{2}{s_{2}-s_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Put</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=s_{2}-s_{1},\qquad C:=\frac{2}{\tau},\qquad\mathcal{A}(s):=\int_{s}^{s_{2}}a(t)\,\,\mathrm{d}t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=s_{2}-s_{1},\qquad C:=\frac{2}{\tau},\qquad\mathcal{A}(s):=\int_{s}^{s_{2}}a(t)\,\,\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Assume for contradiction that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{2a(s)}-\mathcal{A}(s)&gt;C\qquad\text{for every }s\in[s_{1},s_{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for every </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{2a(s)}-\mathcal{A}(s)&gt;C\qquad\text{for every }s\in[s_{1},s_{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(s)&gt;\frac{1}{2}(C+\mathcal{A}(s))^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(s)&gt;\frac{1}{2}(C+\mathcal{A}(s))^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\prime}=-a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\prime}=-a</annotation></semantics></math>, this implies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{1}{C+\mathcal{A}(s)}\right)^{\prime}=\frac{a(s)}{(C+\mathcal{A}(s))^{2}}&gt;\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{1}{C+\mathcal{A}(s)}\right)^{\prime}=\frac{a(s)}{(C+\mathcal{A}(s))^{2}}&gt;\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
