<div id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Li–Yau estimate and (<a href="#S4.E30" title="In 4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="S4.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(59)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}u_{t}\geq\Gamma(u_{t})-\frac{N}{2t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}u_{t}\geq\Gamma(u_{t})-\frac{N}{2t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">First suppose <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim y</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[T_{1},T_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[T_{1},T_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, integrate (<a href="#S4.E59" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) at <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[T_{1},s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[T_{1},s]</annotation></semantics></math> and at <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s,T_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s,T_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Adding the two inequalities and dropping the nonpositive term <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\int_{T_{1}}^{s}\Gamma(u_{t})(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\int_{T_{1}}^{s}\Gamma(u_{t})(x)\,\,\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{T_{1}}(x)-u_{T_{2}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{T_{1}}(x)-u_{T_{2}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{N}{2}\log\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}}+\left\lvert u_{s}(x)-u_{s}(y)\right\rvert-\int_{s}^{T_{2}}\Gamma(u_{t})(y)\,\,\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{N}{2}\log\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}}+\left\lvert u_{s}(x)-u_{s}(y)\right\rvert-\int_{s}^{T_{2}}\Gamma(u_{t})(y)\,\,\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{N}{2}\log\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}}+\sqrt{2\Gamma(u_{s})(y)}-\int_{s}^{T_{2}}\Gamma(u_{t})(y)\,\,\mathrm{d}t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{N}{2}\log\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}}+\sqrt{2\Gamma(u_{s})(y)}-\int_{s}^{T_{2}}\Gamma(u_{t})(y)\,\,\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The second inequality follows from the single-edge contribution to (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2. Preliminary ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). The function <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mapsto\Gamma(u_{s})(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mapsto\Gamma(u_{s})(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous because <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is norm-continuous and <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous quadratic map. Minimising over <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and applying Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 4.5 (One-dimensional optimisation). ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(60)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{T_{1}}(x)-u_{T_{2}}(y)\leq\frac{N}{2}\log\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}}+\frac{2}{T_{2}-T_{1}}\qquad(x\sim y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{T_{1}}(x)-u_{T_{2}}(y)\leq\frac{N}{2}\log\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}}+\frac{2}{T_{2}-T_{1}}\qquad(x\sim y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">For general <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq y</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=x_{0},x_{1},\ldots,x_{\ell}=y" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x_{0},x_{1},\ldots,x_{\ell}=y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">be a geodesic, where <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=\operatorname{dist}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=\operatorname{dist}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Divide <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[T_{1},T_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[T_{1},T_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> equal subintervals and apply (<a href="#S4.E60" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) successively. The logarithmic terms telescope to <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N/2)\log(T_{2}/T_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N/2)\log(T_{2}/T_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, while the spatial terms sum to</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\frac{2}{(T_{2}-T_{1})/\ell}=\frac{2\ell^{2}}{T_{2}-T_{1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\frac{2}{(T_{2}-T_{1})/\ell}=\frac{2\ell^{2}}{T_{2}-T_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">The case <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly by integrating (<a href="#S4.E59" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) and dropping the nonnegative <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> term.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Volume doubling and polynomial growth</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now combine the semigroup smoothing from Subsection <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2. Resolvent smoothing ‣ 3. Point-mass estimates and resolvent smoothing ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, the nonlinear
comparisons from Subsection <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, and the modified-flow Harnack estimate
from Subsection <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. The cutoff–Harnack–mass-conservation architecture is due
to Münch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, Section 4.1]</cite>. Pajot and Russ adapted it to infinite volume by
decomposing the exponential cutoff into a constant background and an <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> perturbation,
and by applying mass conservation only to the latter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, Section 8]</cite>. We use
precisely this infinite-volume device, while replacing the finite-dimensional curvature inputs by
the point-mass and resolvent estimates proved above.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix the parameters from (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2. Preliminary ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E40" title="In Proposition 4.3 (Semigroup comparisons). ‣ 4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>). Put</p>
<table id="S5.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(61)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{*}:=\log(64Nd_{*}),\qquad C:=16N\ell_{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{*}:=\log(64Nd_{*}),\qquad C:=16N\ell_{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="S5.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(62)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{0}:=2\log 2+\frac{N}{2}\log(32d_{*}C^{2})+\frac{N}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{0}:=2\log 2+\frac{N}{2}\log(32d_{*}C^{2})+\frac{N}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The deliberately generous choice of <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> ensures a strict gap.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Parameter gap)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With (<a href="#S5.E61" title="In 5. Volume doubling and polynomial growth ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>)–(<a href="#S5.E62" title="In 5. Volume doubling and polynomial growth ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S5.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(63)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-Q_{0}\geq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-Q_{0}\geq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{*}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{*}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, one has <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 10</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{*}&gt;7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{*}&gt;7</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(16N)\leq\ell_{*},\qquad\log\ell_{*}\leq\frac{\ell_{*}}{2},\qquad\log(32d_{*})\leq\ell_{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(16N)\leq\ell_{*},\qquad\log\ell_{*}\leq\frac{\ell_{*}}{2},\qquad\log(32d_{*})\leq\ell_{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log C\leq\frac{3\ell_{*}}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log C\leq\frac{3\ell_{*}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(32d_{*}C^{2})\leq 4\ell_{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(32d_{*}C^{2})\leq 4\ell_{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{0}\leq 2\log 2+2N\ell_{*}+\frac{N}{2}\leq 3N\ell_{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{0}\leq 2\log 2+2N\ell_{*}+\frac{N}{2}\leq 3N\ell_{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\log 2+N/2\leq N\ell_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\log 2+N/2\leq N\ell_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
