<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The cases <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{*}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{*}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> were settled at the beginning of Section <a href="#S2" title="2. Preliminary ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, so assume <math id="S5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{*}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{*}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="S5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and an integer <math id="S5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</span></p>
