<p id="S5.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in B(x,R_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in B(x,R_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, the Harnack estimate (<a href="#S4.E58" title="In Corollary 4.6 (Modified-flow parabolic Harnack inequality). ‣ 4.2. Li–Yau and Harnack estimates ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), (<a href="#S5.E70" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Volume doubling and polynomial growth ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), and <math id="S5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-t_{0}\geq T/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{0}\geq T/2</annotation></semantics></math> imply</span></p>
