<p id="S5.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}h\subseteq B(x,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}h\subseteq B(x,r)</annotation></semantics></math>, so in particular <math id="S5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\ell^{1}(V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\ell^{1}(V)</annotation></semantics></math>. The background subtraction in (<a href="#S5.E75" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5. Volume doubling and polynomial growth ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>) is essential on an infinite graph: mass conservation is applied only to the integrable perturbation <math id="S5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, never to the constant baseline. By (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2. Preliminary ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>),</span></p>
