<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}(h^{2})-(P_{t}h)^{2}\leq P_{t}h-(P_{t}h)^{2}\leq\frac{1}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}(h^{2})-(P_{t}h)^{2}\leq P_{t}h-(P_{t}h)^{2}\leq\frac{1}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(P_{t}h)\leq\frac{1}{8t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(P_{t}h)\leq\frac{1}{8t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim y</annotation></semantics></math>, the single-edge contribution at <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\bigl(P_{t}h(y)-P_{t}h(x)\bigr)^{2}\leq\Gamma(P_{t}h)(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\bigl(P_{t}h(y)-P_{t}h(x)\bigr)^{2}\leq\Gamma(P_{t}h)(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{t}h(y)-P_{t}h(x)|\leq\frac{1}{2\sqrt{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{t}h(y)-P_{t}h(x)|\leq\frac{1}{2\sqrt{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">Summing along a geodesic from <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the supremum over <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> proves
(<a href="#S6.E81" title="In Lemma 6.1 (Reverse Poincaré and heat-kernel row contraction). ‣ 6.1. Heat-kernel row contraction and exit-time control ‣ 6. Heat-kernel localisation for Poincaré inequalities ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the continuous-time Markov chain with semigroup <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. It can be
realised by rate-<math id="S6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> Poissonisation of the uniformising kernel <math id="S6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+\Delta/d_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+\Delta/d_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Poisson
clock has finitely many rings on every bounded time interval, so the chain is nonexplosive;
the standard construction also gives the strong Markov property. See, for example,
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The exit estimate below is an Ottaviani–Skorokhod-type strong-Markov maximal argument
applied to the first-moment bound furnished by (<a href="#S3.E27" title="In Theorem 3.6 (Laplacian smoothing). ‣ 3.2. Resolvent smoothing ‣ 3. Point-mass estimates and resolvent smoothing ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>); compare
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>. We include the argument because only the weak diffusive bound of
order <math id="S6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{t}/R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{t}/R</annotation></semantics></math> is needed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.2</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Diffusive displacement and exit control)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S6.E82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(82)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x}\operatorname{dist}(x,X_{t})\leq\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x}\operatorname{dist}(x,X_{t})\leq\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{R}:=\inf\{s\geq 0:\operatorname{dist}(x,X_{s})\geq R\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{R}:=\inf\{s\geq 0:\operatorname{dist}(x,X_{s})\geq R\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\geq 4\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\geq 4\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S6.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(83)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{x}(\tau_{R}\leq t)\leq\frac{4\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}}{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{x}(\tau_{R}\leq t)\leq\frac{4\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}}{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, put</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{M}(z):=\min\{\operatorname{dist}(x,z),M\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{M}(z):=\min\{\operatorname{dist}(x,z),M\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">This function is bounded and <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on edges. Hence</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\rho_{M})(z)\leq\frac{1}{2}\sum_{w\sim z}1\leq\frac{d_{*}}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></munder><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\rho_{M})(z)\leq\frac{1}{2}\sum_{w\sim z}1\leq\frac{d_{*}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{M}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{M}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the semigroup estimate (<a href="#S3.E27" title="In Theorem 3.6 (Laplacian smoothing). ‣ 3.2. Resolvent smoothing ‣ 3. Point-mass estimates and resolvent smoothing ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
