<p id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The set <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is finite by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, and</span></p>
