<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 6.1 (Reverse Poincaré and heat-kernel row contraction). ‣ 6.1. Heat-kernel row contraction and exit-time control ‣ 6. Heat-kernel localisation for Poincaré inequalities ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{t}(x,\cdot)-p_{t}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{t}(x,\cdot)-p_{t}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=V</annotation></semantics></math>, there is nothing to compare. Otherwise, every point of <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is at
distance greater than <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Lambda-1)r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Lambda-1)r</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}=2r\sqrt{Nd_{*}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}=2r\sqrt{Nd_{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Lambda-1)r=32\sqrt{Nd_{*}t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Lambda-1)r=32\sqrt{Nd_{*}t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 6.2 (Diffusive displacement and exit control). ‣ 6.1. Heat-kernel row contraction and exit-time control ‣ 6. Heat-kernel localisation for Poincaré inequalities ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> shows that the original walk started at <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> leaves <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> by time
<math id="S6.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at most <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/8</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For completeness, couple the original and censored walks with the same rate-<math id="S6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> Poisson
clock. Whenever their common position is <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, sample a transition according to the
uniformising kernel <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+\Delta/d_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+\Delta/d_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. If the sampled point lies in <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, move both chains there.
If it lies in <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, move only the original chain and keep the censored chain at <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>. After the
first disagreement, continue with any coupling. The censored uniformising kernel has holding
probability</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{\deg_{D}(z)}{d_{*}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{\deg_{D}(z)}{d_{*}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg_{D}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg_{D}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of neighbours of <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Running this kernel at rate
<math id="S6.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the generator (<a href="#S6.E84" title="In 6.2. Censored kernels and localisation ‣ 6. Heat-kernel localisation for Poincaré inequalities ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">84</span></a>). The chains agree until the original
walk leaves <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. By the coupling characterisation of total variation,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{t}^{D}(x,\cdot)-p_{t}(x,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\mathbb{P}_{x}(X_{s}\notin D\text{ for some }s\leq t)\leq\frac{1}{8}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for some </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{t}^{D}(x,\cdot)-p_{t}(x,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\mathbb{P}_{x}(X_{s}\notin D\text{ for some }s\leq t)\leq\frac{1}{8}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the same estimate to <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and using the triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{t}^{D}(x,\cdot)-p_{t}^{D}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\frac{1}{8}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{8}=\frac{3}{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{t}^{D}(x,\cdot)-p_{t}^{D}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\frac{1}{8}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{8}=\frac{3}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma is finite-dimensional and does not use curvature. Its Dobrushin step is
standard, while the posterior-kernel construction packages row overlap in a form adapted to
the variance on the smaller set. It may be viewed as a total-variation analogue of the
pointwise lower-bound step in the preceding heat-kernel arguments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Kernel localisation from row overlap)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be finite, let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subset D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subset D</annotation></semantics></math> be nonempty, and let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be a symmetric Markov
kernel on <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x,y\in B}\|\mathsf{K}(x,\cdot)-\mathsf{K}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\kappa&lt;1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x,y\in B}\|\mathsf{K}(x,\cdot)-\mathsf{K}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\kappa&lt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then every <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:D\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:D\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S6.E86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(86)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x\in B}|f(x)-f_{B}|^{2}\leq\frac{2}{1-\kappa}\left\langle f,(I-\mathsf{K})f\right\rangle_{\ell^{2}(D)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x\in B}|f(x)-f_{B}|^{2}\leq\frac{2}{1-\kappa}\left\langle f,(I-\mathsf{K})f\right\rangle_{\ell^{2}(D)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(z):=\sum_{a\in B}\mathsf{K}(a,z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(z):=\sum_{a\in B}\mathsf{K}(a,z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define a kernel <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Q}(x,y):=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}z\in D\\
s(z)&gt;0\end{subarray}}\frac{\mathsf{K}(x,z)\mathsf{K}(y,z)}{s(z)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Q}(x,y):=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}z\in D\\
s(z)&gt;0\end{subarray}}\frac{\mathsf{K}(x,z)\mathsf{K}(y,z)}{s(z)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">The kernel <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric. It is stochastic because, for <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{y\in B}\mathsf{Q}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{y\in B}\mathsf{Q}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}z\in D\\
s(z)&gt;0\end{subarray}}\mathsf{K}(x,z)\frac{\sum_{y\in B}\mathsf{K}(y,z)}{s(z)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}z\in D\\
s(z)&gt;0\end{subarray}}\mathsf{K}(x,z)\frac{\sum_{y\in B}\mathsf{K}(y,z)}{s(z)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}z\in D\\
s(z)&gt;0\end{subarray}}\mathsf{K}(x,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}z\in D\\
s(z)&gt;0\end{subarray}}\mathsf{K}(x,z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">The last equality holds because <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}(x,z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}(x,z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi(z,y):=\frac{\mathsf{K}(y,z)}{s(z)},\qquad y\in B," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(z,y):=\frac{\mathsf{K}(y,z)}{s(z)},\qquad y\in B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">and choose an arbitrary probability row when <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Regard <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> as a kernel from
<math id="S6.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Q}=\mathsf{K}\Pi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Q}=\mathsf{K}\Pi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">Total variation contracts under a Markov kernel, so</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x,y\in B}\|\mathsf{Q}(x,\cdot)-\mathsf{Q}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\kappa." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x,y\in B}\|\mathsf{Q}(x,\cdot)-\mathsf{Q}(y,\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\kappa.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{osc}(\mathsf{Q}h)\leq\kappa\,\operatorname{osc}(h)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>osc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>osc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{osc}(\mathsf{Q}h)\leq\kappa\,\operatorname{osc}(h)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">for every <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:B\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:B\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the standard Dobrushin oscillation contraction; see
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric and stochastic, it is self-adjoint on the uniform
probability space <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}\equiv 1,\phi_{2},\ldots,\phi_{\#B}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}\equiv 1,\phi_{2},\ldots,\phi_{\#B}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">be an orthonormal eigenbasis, with</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Q}\phi_{j}=\lambda_{j}\phi_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Q}\phi_{j}=\lambda_{j}\phi_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonconstant and</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{j}|\operatorname{osc}(\phi_{j})=\operatorname{osc}(\mathsf{Q}\phi_{j})\leq\kappa\operatorname{osc}(\phi_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>osc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>osc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>osc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{j}|\operatorname{osc}(\phi_{j})=\operatorname{osc}(\mathsf{Q}\phi_{j})\leq\kappa\operatorname{osc}(\phi_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{j}|\leq\kappa." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{j}|\leq\kappa.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Writing</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h-h_{B}=\sum_{j=2}^{\#B}a_{j}\phi_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h-h_{B}=\sum_{j=2}^{\#B}a_{j}\phi_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle h,(I-\mathsf{Q})h\right\rangle_{\ell^{2}(\pi_{B})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle h,(I-\mathsf{Q})h\right\rangle_{\ell^{2}(\pi_{B})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex150.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=2}^{\#B}(1-\lambda_{j})a_{j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=2}^{\#B}(1-\lambda_{j})a_{j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\kappa)\sum_{j=2}^{\#B}a_{j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\kappa)\sum_{j=2}^{\#B}a_{j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\kappa)\operatorname{Var}_{\pi_{B}}(h)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\kappa)\operatorname{Var}_{\pi_{B}}(h).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S6.E87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(87)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}_{\pi_{B}}(h)\leq\frac{1}{1-\kappa}\left\langle h,(I-\mathsf{Q})h\right\rangle_{\ell^{2}(\pi_{B})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}_{\pi_{B}}(h)\leq\frac{1}{1-\kappa}\left\langle h,(I-\mathsf{Q})h\right\rangle_{\ell^{2}(\pi_{B})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to compare the two Dirichlet forms. Let <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be uniform on <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Conditional on
