<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3. </span>A fixed-dilation Poincaré inequality</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now apply the overlap estimate from Subsection <a href="#S6.SS2" title="6.2. Censored kernels and localisation ‣ 6. Heat-kernel localisation for Poincaré inequalities ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> to the censored heat
semigroup. Spectral calculus turns one-step dissipation into edge energy and yields the
fixed-dilation inequality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.5</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fixed-dilation Poincaré inequality)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption B. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> hold and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{*}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{*}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> be given by
(<a href="#S6.E85" title="In Lemma 6.3 (Censored finite-volume row overlap). ‣ 6.2. Censored kernels and localisation ‣ 6. Heat-kernel localisation for Poincaré inequalities ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">85</span></a>). Then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

