<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Bounded maximum principle on an infinite graph</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The nonlinear gradient estimate in Subsection <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1. The modified heat equation ‣ 4. Modified heat, Li–Yau, and Harnack estimates ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> requires a maximum principle on an infinite
vertex set, where the supremum need not be attained. The following bounded version uses
approximate maximisers and an upper Dini derivative; no volume-growth hypothesis is needed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
