<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t+\tau_{n}}(x_{n})\geq H(t+\tau_{n})-\tau_{n}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t+\tau_{n}}(x_{n})\geq H(t+\tau_{n})-\tau_{n}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable in <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex210" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t+\tau_{n}}=h_{t}+\tau_{n}\partial_{t}h_{t}+o(\tau_{n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t+\tau_{n}}=h_{t}+\tau_{n}\partial_{t}h_{t}+o(\tau_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">in <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. The same expansion shows that <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex211" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}(x_{n})\geq H(t)-O(\tau_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}(x_{n})\geq H(t)-O(\tau_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is an approximate maximiser of <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex212" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{H(t+\tau_{n})-H(t)}{\tau_{n}}\leq\partial_{t}h_{t}(x_{n})+o(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{H(t+\tau_{n})-H(t)}{\tau_{n}}\leq\partial_{t}h_{t}(x_{n})+o(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the limsup and then letting the approximation level tend to zero proves
(<a href="#A1.E94" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Bounded maximum principle on an infinite graph ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">94</span></a>).
For every <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in the set on the right-hand side of (<a href="#A1.E94" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Bounded maximum principle on an infinite graph ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">94</span></a>) and every <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex213" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}(y)-h_{t}(x)\leq\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}(y)-h_{t}(x)\leq\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex214" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}h_{t}(x)\leq M\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}h_{t}(x)\leq M\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Letting <math id="A1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E94" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Bounded maximum principle on an infinite graph ‣ Nonnegative Bakry–Émery Curvature on Bounded-Degree Graphs Implies Volume Doubling and Poincaré Inequalities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">94</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex215" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{+}H(t)\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{+}H(t)\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">Since</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex216" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|H(t)-H(s)|\leq\|h_{t}-h_{s}\|_{\infty}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|H(t)-H(s)|\leq\|h_{t}-h_{s}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="A1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz and hence absolutely continuous. At
almost every time it is differentiable, and there</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex217" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\prime}(t)=D^{+}H(t)\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\prime}(t)=D^{+}H(t)\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.13.1" class="ltx_text">Integration shows that <math id="A1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing. No attainment of the supremum and no volume
hypothesis are required.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
